BREACHWATCH
McGraw Hill — IG-2026-026

Status: 🟠 Confirmed / Data publicly distributed
Priority: CRITICAL
Sector: Education / Publishing
Region: Global
Platform: Salesforce
Threat Actor: ShinyHunters — claimed
Primary Failure: SaaS configuration / public-facing access control
Last Reviewed: August 18, 2026

McGraw Hill confirmed unauthorized access to information available through a Salesforce-hosted webpage and linked the incident to a broader Salesforce configuration issue affecting multiple organizations. McGraw Hill said its Salesforce accounts, core customer databases, courseware, and internal systems were not directly compromised.

More than 100 GB of information was later distributed publicly. HIBP identified approximately 13.5 million unique email addresses, with some records also containing names, phone numbers, and physical addresses.

Confirmed
Unauthorized access occurred.
A Salesforce-hosted webpage was involved.
McGraw Hill attributed the incident to a broader Salesforce configuration issue.
Data was subsequently publicly distributed.
Approximately 13.5M unique email addresses appear in the released dataset.
Names, phones, and physical addresses occur in portions of the dataset.
Claimed

ShinyHunters claimed approximately 45 million Salesforce records and responsibility for the extortion activity.

